<title>Hairline Fund Release &amp; Payments Brief</title>
<link rel=3D"stylesheet" href=3D"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=
=3DIBM+Plex+Sans:wght@400;500;600&amp;family=3DIBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;500&a=
mp;display=3Dswap">


<main>
<header>
  <p class=3D"eyebrow">Hairline =C2=B7 Admin dashboard =C2=B7 Requirements<=
/p>
  <h1>Fund release, payout rails, patient payment options and cancellation =
fees</h1>
  <p class=3D"meta">For the project manager and dev team. Status column is =
from a code audit of hairline-backend, hairline-frontend and the Flutter ap=
p on 8 Sept 2026, on the current branches. Companion document: <em>Hairline=
 =E2=80=94 Payment Routing Spec (developer) v1.0</em>.</p>
  <div class=3D"key">
    <span>Status key:</span>
    <span class=3D"pill ok">Built</span><span>exists and is wired end to en=
d</span>
    <span class=3D"pill warn">Partial</span><span>something exists but does=
n't meet the requirement</span>
    <span class=3D"pill bad">Not built</span><span>nothing in the codebase<=
/span>
  </div>
</header>

<p class=3D"lede">Headline: the payments <em>configuration</em> layer is la=
rgely built (commission, deposit rate, instalments, saved cards, payout sta=
tements). The <em>money movement</em> layer is not: there is no hold-and-re=
lease, no Stripe Connect, no automated settlement run, and the patient app =
can't yet pick a payment plan. Sections A and B are almost entirely new wor=
k. C and D are partly built but need reworking against the spec.</p>

<h2><span class=3D"sec">A</span>Fund release mechanism</h2>
<p>Provider marks the treatment complete =E2=86=92 patient is asked to conf=
irm =E2=86=92 if no response within the configured window the funds release=
 automatically =E2=86=92 release goes out on whichever rail the provider is=
 on.</p>

<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<tbody><tr><th>Requirement</th><th>Status</th><th>What exists today</th><th=
>What to build</th></tr>
<tr><td class=3D"req">1. Provider marks treatment as complete</td><td class=
=3D"st"><span class=3D"pill warn">Partial</span></td>
<td class=3D"now">Provider has an "End Treatment" action (<code>POST /treat=
ment-execution/{id}/complete</code>, also <code>end-treatment</code>). It m=
oves the booking to <code>completed</code> and writes an audit row. Nothing=
 downstream listens to it for money.</td>
<td>Treat this as the trigger event. Emit a domain event on completion that=
 starts the confirmation clock. Rename the provider-facing button to "Mark =
treatment complete" and show what happens next (patient confirmation, relea=
se date).</td></tr>
<tr><td class=3D"req">2. Patient gets email + push asking them to confirm</=
td><td class=3D"st"><span class=3D"pill bad">Not built</span></td>
<td class=3D"now">A <code>TreatmentCompletedNotification</code> class exist=
s (mail + push channels) but it's post-op instructions, and it is never dis=
patched from production code. The Flutter app has no confirm-completion scr=
een; notifications are bucketed by string-matching on the title.</td>
<td>New notification "Please confirm your treatment is complete" with a dee=
p link. New Flutter screen with Confirm / Raise a problem. New endpoints: <=
code>POST /bookings/{id}/confirm-completion</code> and <code>POST /bookings=
/{id}/dispute</code>. Store <code>patient_confirmed_at</code>, <code>confir=
mation_deadline_at</code>, <code>disputed_at</code> on the booking.</td></t=
r>
<tr><td class=3D"req">3. Auto-release if the patient doesn't respond, windo=
w adjustable in admin settings (e.g. 48h =E2=86=92 72h)</td><td class=3D"st=
"><span class=3D"pill bad">Not built</span></td>
<td class=3D"now">No hold/release concept anywhere. No setting for it. The =
scheduler already runs ~18 daily commands (quote expiry, overdue instalment=
s, slot holds) so the pattern is there.</td>
<td>Admin setting <code>completion_confirmation_window_hours</code> (defaul=
t 72) editable under Settings =E2=86=92 Billing. Daily (or hourly) command =
<code>bookings:auto-release-completed</code>: any booking past its deadline=
 with no dispute =E2=86=92 mark <code>release_approved</code> and hand to t=
he payout rail. A raised dispute pauses the clock until an admin resolves i=
t.</td></tr>
<tr><td class=3D"req">4a. Released funds go out via Stripe Connect where th=
e provider has it</td><td class=3D"st"><span class=3D"pill bad">Not built</=
span></td>
<td class=3D"now">See section B. No connected accounts exist.</td>
<td>On release: <code>payouts.create</code> on the provider's connected acc=
ount for <code>clinic_share</code>. Record the payout id on the booking led=
ger.</td></tr>
<tr><td class=3D"req">4b. Otherwise it joins a settlement cycle (e.g. Mon=
=E2=80=93Sun collected, paid the following Wednesday), paid manually by us =
or via the Revolut Business API</td><td class=3D"st"><span class=3D"pill wa=
rn">Partial</span></td>
<td class=3D"now">A payout-statement engine exists: <code>payout_statements=
</code> with statuses <code>readiness =E2=86=92 approved =E2=86=92 processi=
ng =E2=86=92 paid / failed / overdue / voided</code>, per-provider schedule=
 <code>weekly | bimonthly | monthly</code>, approve and retry in the admin =
UI with re-auth. But statements are only generated by an admin calling the =
API for one provider and a date range. There is no scheduled batch, no "mar=
k as paid" button (the API exists as <code>transfer-result</code>), and no =
Revolut integration at all. Row actions on the list page other than "view" =
are still simulated.</td>
<td>Scheduled command that closes each cycle and generates statements for e=
very manual-rail provider. Admin settings: <code>settlement_period</code> (=
weekly), <code>settlement_cutoff_day</code> (Sunday), <code>payout_day</cod=
e> (Wednesday). Wire the "Mark as paid" and bulk-approve buttons to the rea=
l API. Revolut Business API as a second step: create the payment from the a=
pproved statement, poll status, set paid/failed automatically.</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>

<div class=3D"callout">
<p><b>Conflict to resolve before build.</b> This note says the confirmation=
 window is 48=E2=80=9372 hours. The routing spec defines Completion as "cli=
nic marks complete AND (patient confirms OR 7 days pass with no dispute)", =
and the structuring summary talks about a ~7 day dispute window. Pick one n=
umber as the default and make it one setting. My recommendation: one settin=
g, default 72h, and drop the separate 7-day figure from the spec.</p>
<p><b>Second one.</b> The documented booking state machine (<code>docs/doma=
in/booking-states.md</code>) treats "Completed" as the end of aftercare aft=
er a medical-supervisor review. For payment purposes "complete" has to mean=
 the procedure was performed. Define the release trigger as the procedure-c=
omplete event, not the end of the aftercare programme, and fix the docs, be=
cause the code's status enum already disagrees with them.</p>
</div>

<h2><span class=3D"sec">B</span>Payment providers and types</h2>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<tbody><tr><th>Requirement</th><th>Status</th><th>What exists today</th><th=
>What to build</th></tr>
<tr><td class=3D"req">1. Stripe UK only for all patients at launch</td><td =
class=3D"st"><span class=3D"pill warn">Partial</span></td>
<td class=3D"now">Charges are plain platform PaymentIntents. There is a "St=
ripe accounts" settings page, but it holds per-country <em>platform</em> ke=
ys (<code>stripe_default</code>, <code>stripe_us</code>, <code>stripe_sg</c=
ode>) and routes patients between them. That is multi-account routing, not =
Connect.</td>
<td>Configure a single UK platform account (Hairline App Ltd) and disable t=
he per-country routing for launch. Keep the mechanism for the Ireland/EU ac=
count later.</td></tr>
<tr><td class=3D"req">2. Add Stripe Ireland/EU when volume justifies it</td=
><td class=3D"st"><span class=3D"pill ok">Built</span></td>
<td class=3D"now">The multi-account routing above handles this once the Iri=
sh entity and account exist.</td>
<td>Nothing now. Trigger is in the structuring summary (EU volume &gt; ~50/=
month for a quarter).</td></tr>
<tr><td class=3D"req">3. Provider chooses payout rail at onboarding: Stripe=
 Connect (UK/EEA billing entity) or manual payments</td><td class=3D"st"><s=
pan class=3D"pill bad">Not built</span></td>
<td class=3D"now">Providers have bank details only (IBAN, SWIFT, routing). =
No <code>payout_method</code> field, no Connect onboarding, no Account Link=
s, no transfers, no destination charges. Only <em>affiliates</em> have a pa=
yout-method choice. Note: providers are created by admins, there is no prov=
ider self-signup, so "at signup" means the admin Add Provider flow plus the=
 provider's own Billing settings tab.</td>
<td>Add <code>payout_method</code> on providers: <code>stripe_connect | man=
ual_bank</code> (Revolut later as a manual-rail sub-type). Add a "Payout me=
thod" step in Add Provider and in provider Billing settings. Connect onboar=
ding: Express or Custom account, <code>payouts.schedule.interval =3D manual=
</code>, onboarding via Account Links, store <code>acct_id</code>, billing-=
entity country and contract currency. Show Connect status (onboarding compl=
ete, payouts enabled, requirements due) in the admin provider view. Everyth=
ing else in the routing spec (destination charges, transfers at T-60, rever=
sals on reschedule) hangs off this.</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>

<h2><span class=3D"sec">C</span>Patient payment options</h2>
<p>Full detail is in the Payment Routing Spec. Status of the pieces it reli=
es on:</p>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<tbody><tr><th>Spec requirement</th><th>Status</th><th>What exists today</t=
h><th>What to build</th></tr>
<tr><td class=3D"req">Full payment (1a / 1b)</td><td class=3D"st"><span cla=
ss=3D"pill warn">Partial</span></td>
<td class=3D"now">Deposit percentage defaults to 100% when no override, so =
full payment works. No T-60 transfer job (1b) because there is no Connect.<=
/td><td>T-60 daily job once Connect exists.</td></tr>
<tr><td class=3D"req">Deposit + balance, balance auto-charged at T-30 (opti=
on 2)</td><td class=3D"st"><span class=3D"pill warn">Partial</span></td>
<td class=3D"now">Bookings carry deposit amount/percentage, remaining amoun=
t, payment deadline (=3D appointment =E2=88=92 30 days). Deposit rate is ad=
min-configurable globally and per provider, and check-in is blocked while a=
 balance is outstanding. But there is no T-30 job that charges the balance =
and no dedicated pay-balance endpoint. Saved-card charging exists but never=
 sets <code>off_session: true</code>, so Stripe treats it as a customer-pre=
sent charge (more 3DS challenges, more declines).</td>
<td>T-30 daily job creating the off-session balance charge with Smart Retri=
es, patient notifications, cancel at T-21 if unpaid. Fix the off-session fl=
ag. Add a pay-balance endpoint for patients who want to pay early.</td></tr=
>
<tr><td class=3D"req">Instalments (option 3)</td><td class=3D"st"><span cla=
ss=3D"pill ok">Built</span></td>
<td class=3D"now">Instalment schedule, admin config (enable, counts 2=E2=80=
=939, cutoff days, minimum amount, first-instalment type, grace period), da=
ily overdue-charge command with 3 retries, payment-due reminders. Last inst=
alment must land =E2=89=A5 30 days pre-procedure.</td><td>Only the clinic-s=
hare transfer at T-30 once fully paid (Connect dependency).</td></tr>
<tr><td class=3D"req">Patient chooses a plan at checkout</td><td class=3D"s=
t"><span class=3D"pill bad">Not built</span></td>
<td class=3D"now">The Flutter app has one Stripe PaymentSheet flow. The dep=
osit-percentage parameter is commented out and there is no plan picker. Adm=
in can configure plans that no patient can select.</td><td>Plan selection s=
creen in the app (full / deposit / instalments, with the schedule preview t=
he backend already returns). This is the biggest patient-facing gap.</td></=
tr>
<tr><td class=3D"req">Record actual Stripe fees per booking from <code>bala=
nce_transaction</code></td><td class=3D"st"><span class=3D"pill bad">Not bu=
ilt</span></td>
<td class=3D"now">Payments snapshot commission rate, commission amount and =
FX rate. No processing-fee capture anywhere.</td><td>Webhook handlers for <=
code>charge.succeeded</code>, <code>charge.refunded</code>, <code>transfer.=
created</code>, <code>payout.paid</code> that fetch the balance transaction=
 and store <code>fee</code> and <code>fee_details</code>. Per-booking ledge=
r per spec =C2=A72.4.</td></tr>
<tr><td class=3D"req">Commission rate, config per clinic, default 20%</td><=
td class=3D"st"><span class=3D"pill ok">Built</span></td>
<td class=3D"now">Global rate plus per-provider overrides with effective da=
tes, audit log, snapshots on booking, payment and payout statement.</td><td=
>Housekeeping: there are two competing global rates (<code>set_commissions<=
/code> and <code>payment_configurations.commission_rate</code>). Only the f=
irst is used. Remove or hide the second.</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>

<h2><span class=3D"sec">D</span>Cancellation fees for patients and provider=
s</h2>
<p>We need multiple configurable cancellation points, keyed on days before =
the appointment. Example ladder (not the final numbers):</p>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<tbody><tr><th>Days before appointment</th><th>Cancellation fee</th><th>Pat=
ient gets back</th></tr>
<tr><td class=3D"num">30 or more</td><td class=3D"num">20%</td><td class=3D=
"num">80%</td></tr>
<tr><td class=3D"num">3 to 29</td><td class=3D"num">50%</td><td class=3D"nu=
m">50%</td></tr>
<tr><td class=3D"num">0 to 2</td><td class=3D"num">100%</td><td class=3D"nu=
m">0%</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>

<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<tbody><tr><th>Requirement</th><th>Status</th><th>What exists today</th><th=
>What to build</th></tr>
<tr><td class=3D"req">Configurable, multi-tier ladder</td><td class=3D"st">=
<span class=3D"pill warn">Partial</span></td>
<td class=3D"now">A ladder exists but is hardcoded in <code>BookingCancella=
tionService</code>: &gt;30 days 90% refund, 15=E2=80=9330 days 50%, &lt;15 =
days 0%. The admin refund modal repeats the same three tiers as literal tex=
t. The only setting is a free-text "cancellation policy" paragraph shown on=
 quotes. The patient app's cancellation policy screen is lorem ipsum.</td>
<td>New table <code>cancellation_fee_tiers</code>: <code>days_before_min</c=
ode>, <code>days_before_max</code>, <code>fee_percent</code>, <code>applies=
_to (patient | provider)</code>, <code>provider_id</code> nullable for per-=
clinic overrides, effective dates, audit log. Admin page under Settings =E2=
=86=92 Billing to edit the ladder. Refund service reads tiers instead of co=
nstants. Patient app shows the fee and the refund amount before the patient=
 confirms a cancellation, and renders the real policy text.</td></tr>
<tr><td class=3D"req">Fee is modelled as a fee, not just a smaller refund</=
td><td class=3D"st"><span class=3D"pill bad">Not built</span></td>
<td class=3D"now">The withheld amount is never recorded as a fee, never spl=
it between Hairline and the clinic, never reaches a payout statement.</td>
<td>Record <code>cancellation_fee_amount</code> and its split. Contract que=
stion below decides the split.</td></tr>
<tr><td class=3D"req">Works with deposit and instalment plans</td><td class=
=3D"st"><span class=3D"pill bad">Not built</span></td>
<td class=3D"now">Refund is a percentage of the total, applied to whatever =
was actually paid, and future instalments are cancelled.</td>
<td>Rule: fee =3D tier% =C3=97 price. If paid-so-far =E2=89=A5 fee, refund =
the difference. If paid-so-far &lt; fee (deposit plan, early instalments), =
charge the shortfall to the saved card, and say so in the patient terms. Ca=
ncellation within a deposit plan before the balance is charged at 30+ days =
is exactly the deposit, which is why 20% is the right first tier.</td></tr>
<tr><td class=3D"req">Provider-side cancellation</td><td class=3D"st"><span=
 class=3D"pill bad">Not built</span></td>
<td class=3D"now">Nothing. Providers have a cancel action with no consequen=
ce.</td>
<td>Needs a definition first (see decisions). Minimum: full refund to the p=
atient, fee charged to the clinic and deducted from its next payout stateme=
nt.</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>

<h2><span class=3D"sec">E</span>Decisions needed from us</h2>
<ol class=3D"decisions">
<li><b>Confirmation window default.</b> 72 hours or 7 days. One setting, on=
e number in the contracts.</li>
<li><b>What a provider pays when the provider cancels.</b> Percentage of th=
e price, fixed amount, or just the patient's refund plus Hairline's process=
ing costs. This is a clinic-contract term, so it goes into the framework ag=
reement (HS-95) at the same time.</li>
<li><b>Who keeps the patient cancellation fee.</b> All to the clinic, all t=
o Hairline, or split at the commission rate. The ladder in patient terms an=
d the clinic framework must say the same thing (structuring summary =C2=A74=
).</li>
<li><b>Global ladder only at launch, or per-clinic overrides on day one.</b=
> Build the table with a nullable provider id either way; ship the UI for g=
lobal first.</li>
<li><b>Revolut now or later.</b> Manual "mark as paid" gets us live. The Re=
volut Business API is a separate ticket and only matters once statement vol=
ume is annoying.</li>
</ol>

<h2><span class=3D"sec">F</span>Settings to add to the admin dashboard</h2>
<div class=3D"tbl"><table>
<tbody><tr><th>Setting</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Used by</th></t=
r>
<tr><td><code>completion_confirmation_window_hours</code></td><td>number</t=
d><td class=3D"num">72</td><td>Auto-release job (A3)</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>settlement_period</code></td><td>weekly | bimonthly | monthly=
</td><td>weekly</td><td>Statement generator (A4b)</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>settlement_cutoff_day</code></td><td>weekday</td><td>Sunday</=
td><td>Statement generator</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>payout_day</code></td><td>weekday</td><td>Wednesday</td><td>S=
tatement due date, provider "next payout" display</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>payout_method</code> (per provider)</td><td>stripe_connect | =
manual_bank</td><td>manual_bank</td><td>Release routing (A4)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Cancellation fee tiers</td><td>table, editable ladder</td><td>20 / =
50 / 100 example</td><td>Refund service, patient app (D)</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>balance_charge_days_before</code></td><td>number</td><td clas=
s=3D"num">30</td><td>T-30 job (C)</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>balance_unpaid_cancel_days_before</code></td><td>number</td><=
td class=3D"num">21</td><td>T-21 cancel (C)</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>

<h2><span class=3D"sec">G</span>Suggested build order</h2>
<ol>
<li>Cancellation tiers table + admin page + refund service reading it. Smal=
l, self-contained, and unblocks the legal drafts (HS-96).</li>
<li>Completion confirmation: event, patient notification and app screen, di=
spute endpoint, auto-release job, the window setting. This is the core of s=
ection A and needs no Stripe work.</li>
<li>Settlement cycle: scheduled statement generation, real "mark as paid" a=
nd bulk approve, cycle settings. Gets manual-rail clinics (Turkey) paid cor=
rectly from day one.</li>
<li>Patient plan picker in the Flutter app, the T-30 balance job, off-sessi=
on fix, fee capture from balance transactions.</li>
<li>Stripe Connect: provider payout method, onboarding, destination charges=
, T-60 transfers, release via payouts. Largest piece and only needed once a=
 UK/EEA-entity clinic signs.</li>
<li>Revolut Business API for the manual rail.</li>
</ol>

<p class=3D"foot">Sources: hairline-backend, hairline-frontend, hairline-ap=
p-2 at branch <code>claude/admin-dashboard-payments-fptqlo</code>; Hairline=
 Structuring Summary (Jul=E2=80=93Sep 2026); Payment Routing Spec v1.0.</p>
</main>

